WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:11.168
In tutorial 3.2, you'll show readers and
search engines who stands behind your

00:00:11.218 --> 00:00:12.076
pages.

00:00:13.107 --> 00:00:17.167
First, in Website settings,
open the Author and profile tab.

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:20.585
Profile readiness, on the right,
shows what's still missing.

00:00:21.584 --> 00:00:25.384
Not sure what to write? How to fill
this in walks you through each part.

00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:32.529
Next, add the author. Type the
real person's name and job title,

00:00:32.579 --> 00:00:34.934
then their credentials and a short bio.

00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:41.994
Add their author page, profile links like
LinkedIn, and the topics they know well.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.205
If someone qualified checks your pages,
add them as your expert reviewer.

00:00:49.255 --> 00:00:51.485
Your pages then show Reviewed by.

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:58.159
Then add your business contact details,
like your phone and opening hours.

00:00:58.209 --> 00:01:00.563
They must match your
Google Business Profile.

00:01:02.555 --> 00:01:06.730
If customers visit you, add your
address and the areas you serve.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.648
Now every item in Profile
readiness is ticked.

00:01:11.605 --> 00:01:13.719
Finally, click Save profile.

00:01:16.559 --> 00:01:19.784
From then on, every new page
carries the author's name,

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:22.434
a short author box and your reviewer.

00:01:22.484 --> 00:01:27.184
Your contact details and address go into
each page's contact block and your local

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:30.368
pages. You'll see it
all on the Content page.

00:01:31.373 --> 00:01:35.743
So, open Author and profile,
add the author, add a reviewer,

00:01:35.793 --> 00:01:39.177
add your contact details and
address, and save the profile.

00:01:40.181 --> 00:01:45.222
Your profile is ready. Next, set
your style guide in tutorial 3.3.
